Apache Geode is a data management platform that provides real-time,
consistent access to data-intensive applications throughout widely
distributed cloud architectures.  It is the open source core of what was
commercially known as GemFire.

Geode pools memory, CPU, network resources and optionally local disk across
multiple processes to manage application objects and behavior.  Data is
kept in regions, which are replicated or partitioned across the members of
a cluster for high availability, scalability and fault tolerance.
Features include:

- in-memory key/value regions with optional persistence and overflow to
  disk
- OQL queries, continuous queries and Lucene based full text indexes
- transactions, event notification and guaranteed message delivery
- WAN replication between clusters
- client/server topology with Java and native (C++, .NET) clients
- gfsh command line shell, Pulse web monitoring and a management REST API
